Hardware YubiKeys cannot be attached from a browser tab, and the YubiKey
driver stack (ykcore, USB/PCSC backends, QtConcurrent discovery) is not
compiled into the wasm build. Replace the driver include with a local
YubiKeySlot typedef and make challenge() fail cleanly. Challenge-response
keys can still be listed in a database; unlocking with one reports a clear
error instead of failing to link.

The stub header no longer pulls in <QIODevice> transitively (the driver
header did), so add it directly to the .cpp where QDataStream needs it.

--- a/src/keys/ChallengeResponseKey.h
+++ b/src/keys/ChallengeResponseKey.h
@@ -19,8 +19,18 @@
 #ifndef KPXC_CHALLENGE_RESPONSE_KEY_H
 #define KPXC_CHALLENGE_RESPONSE_KEY_H
 
+#include <QDataStream>
+#include <QPair>
+
+#include <botan/secmem.h>
+
 #include "Key.h"
-#include "drivers/YubiKey.h"
+
+// WebAssembly build: hardware YubiKeys cannot be attached from a browser
+// tab and the YubiKey driver stack is not compiled in. The slot type is
+// kept so serialized keys still round-trip; challenge() always fails
+// cleanly with an error message.
+typedef QPair<unsigned int, int> YubiKeySlot;
 
 class ChallengeResponseKey : public Key
 {
